<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48793" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">trans-frĕto</span></b> , āvi,
			ātum, 1, v. n. and <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a.</i> [fretum], <i>to
				cross a strait</i>, <i>pass over the sea</i>
			(post-Aug.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense5"><b>(a).</b>
			<i>Neutr.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quam primum transfretaturi (Brundisium),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Caes. 34</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">Gell. 10, 26, 1</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Amm. 22, 6, 4</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Vulg. Luc. 8,
				22</span></i>.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense5"><b>(b).</b>
			<i>Act.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">transfretabantur in dies noctesque navibus
					ratibusque,</span>”
				<i>were ferried over</i>, <i>put across</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 31, 4, 5</span></i>
			.— * </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vitae conversationem sine gubernaculo rationis
					transfretantes,</span>”
				i. e. <i>passing through</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. Poen. 1</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
